1
00:00:03,169 --> 00:00:04,373
Good evening, everyone.

2
00:00:04,392 --> 00:00:06,378
I trust you've had a fruitful day.

3
00:00:06,418 --> 00:00:09,224
I do not say happy, though I hope it has been happy.

4
00:00:09,265 --> 00:00:17,684
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Samha Sambuddhosa

5
00:00:18,509 --> 00:00:26,256
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambuddhasa.

6
00:00:27,077 --> 00:00:35,625
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambuddhasa.

7
00:00:35,645 --> 00:00:39,808
Homage to the Buddha, the blessed, noble and fully self-awakened one.

8
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:48,076
So we were looking at this discourse, the Kittagiri discourse, where we came across these two characters.

9
00:00:48,984 --> 00:00:52,752
Asaji and Punas, what was his name?

10
00:00:53,713 --> 00:00:56,719
I've forgotten his name.

11
00:00:56,738 --> 00:00:58,040
And they were miscreants.

12
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,651
They were untrained monks and all that sort of stuff.

13
00:01:04,632 --> 00:01:06,396
And the Buddha has a go at them, if you remember.

14
00:01:06,536 --> 00:01:12,867
And then he takes the opportunity to talk about seven types of individuals.

15
00:01:13,893 --> 00:01:24,310
So these have been nicely categorized here by Shahrukh Rajel, Pressing Out Pure Honey, nice little book as accompaniment to the Majjhima Nikaya, the Middle and Saint.

16
00:01:25,031 --> 00:01:28,495
So now, there are two interesting things here to note.

17
00:01:28,697 --> 00:01:31,460
The first one is what's called a personal witness.

18
00:01:31,561 --> 00:01:38,873
They abide by the formless attainments and, sorry, liberated both ways, excuse me, number one, liberated in both ways.

19
00:01:39,353 --> 00:01:40,896
So these are the people

20
00:01:41,111 --> 00:01:46,980
who through the jhana and through vipassana attain liberation.

21
00:01:47,641 --> 00:01:55,233
And the liberated by wisdom, that's category number two, don't have to go through the jhana, they're liberated by wisdom.

22
00:01:55,332 --> 00:01:56,474
So these are the arahants.

23
00:01:57,316 --> 00:02:06,950
Now the rest all belong to the other three categories, the stream entrant, the first attainment, the once returner and the non-returner.

24
00:02:07,876 --> 00:02:21,215
So the first one is that they, much the same as number one, they use the jhanas and vipassana, but all the defilements and not all the taints are not completely destroyed.

25
00:02:22,257 --> 00:02:33,954
And then there's those who are without attaining those jhanas, but who review and examine with wisdom the teachings of the Buddha.

26
00:02:33,973 --> 00:02:36,076
So they also make a path.

27
00:02:36,225 --> 00:02:42,012
Then there's the ones liberated by faith without abiding in the formless attainments.

28
00:02:42,051 --> 00:02:52,682
In other words, without the jhana, without the absorptions, with some tanks destroyed, but they have faith, is planted, rooted and established in the Buddha.

29
00:02:53,364 --> 00:02:55,466
So this is the second thing.

30
00:02:55,545 --> 00:02:57,989
The first one is that you don't need the jhana.

31
00:02:58,909 --> 00:03:04,816
Remember that as lay people, it's very difficult to find the time and space to practice those absorptions.

32
00:03:04,836 --> 00:03:05,997
You've got to give your heart to it.

33
00:03:06,617 --> 00:03:29,233
but vipassana is very straightforward and can be done very easily as a lay person the other thing is the one by faith now confidence confidence a better word um you don't need the intellect so you don't need to be thinking uh about the buddha's teachings to some sort of fine degree

34
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:59,406
it's much more about about having confidence and what that confidence does is it it opens you up to to to view to investigate uh now people who don't have that confidence suffer from doubt they doubt the buddha was fully liberated the doubt that dharma really is going to go anywhere they doubt the teacher whom they're under and they cause doubt themselves all this doubt is overcome when one has confidence

35
00:04:00,094 --> 00:04:02,336
So confidence is a root thing.

36
00:04:02,837 --> 00:04:05,639
It belongs to the five spiritual faculties.

37
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:09,343
It begins with this confidence.

38
00:04:09,364 --> 00:04:23,317
Then one puts the effort in, then one establishes the awareness, then the concentration rises quite naturally out of that interest and the wisdom factor is enlivened.

39
00:04:23,336 --> 00:04:28,802
That's the intuitive intelligence which is brought in to see the three characteristics.

40
00:04:31,836 --> 00:04:56,595
or suffering and not self so you can see that there are certain people who don't have to be you know always investigating reading about the dharma or anything it's good enough just to do the vipassana and then there are those that are planted right okay then there's the dharma followers

41
00:04:58,786 --> 00:05:03,173
These are the ones who abide, who don't have the jhana again.

42
00:05:04,495 --> 00:05:15,290
And the tents have not yet been destroyed, but they have a reflective acceptance of the teaching of the Buddha and those five faculties.

43
00:05:15,331 --> 00:05:17,694
So that's the receptive acceptance.

44
00:05:18,896 --> 00:05:23,723
That's more in the sense of an intellectual acceptance.

45
00:05:23,742 --> 00:05:26,127
Again, there's no big need for that person.

46
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:31,646
to have a PhD in the Dharma.

47
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:33,406
And finally, there are the faith followers.

48
00:05:33,528 --> 00:05:47,041
So abiding without, again, abiding in those jhanic states, the tanks have not yet been destroyed, but they have enough faith and love for the Buddha and the five spiritual faculties.

49
00:05:47,762 --> 00:05:54,730
So what these categories of seven people tell us is, first of all, you don't need the jhana.

50
00:05:55,081 --> 00:06:00,112
and B, you don't need to be highly intellectual at all.

51
00:06:01,206 --> 00:06:29,458
one big story that supports this of course is the is the monk who joined who really didn't have much uh upstairs and um his brother actually said to him it was better for him to you know leave the order and do something useful and when the buddha heard this he went to see him and gave him a very simple exercise of taking a fresh piece of cloth rubbing it wiping the sweat off his face and things like that and constantly saying impermanence

52
00:06:29,742 --> 00:06:59,343
impermanent everything's impermanent and would you believe it in no length of time he was fully liberated so uh it's good to know that you know we don't have to be big intellects to become liberated in fact it's often a big barrier so there's another story about that where um a very good teacher had all his students or many of his students were became fully liberated but he wasn't

53
00:06:59,762 --> 00:07:03,307
So after a while, he thought to himself, well, you know, why is that?

54
00:07:03,387 --> 00:07:08,654
And he sort of ate a humble pie and he went to see one of his students.

55
00:07:08,694 --> 00:07:12,961
And his students, this particular student thought, no, this teacher's too conceited.

56
00:07:13,021 --> 00:07:16,146
You know, whatever I say, he won't open up to it.

57
00:07:16,165 --> 00:07:17,747
So I'll pass him on to somebody else.

58
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:21,612
So he said to him, actually, the person who really helped you is so-and-so.

59
00:07:22,113 --> 00:07:27,762
And in this way, he was passed along the line of all his students until one student said to him,

60
00:07:28,079 --> 00:07:32,045
Why don't you go with this young boy and he'll give you the trick, you see.

61
00:07:32,927 --> 00:07:41,904
So this was a big humiliating thing to have to go to a young child for guidance in the spiritual life.

62
00:07:43,228 --> 00:07:45,872
And the young child took him to a termite hill.

63
00:07:46,774 --> 00:07:51,403
Now it seems that when termite hills are empty of termites, snakes live in them.

64
00:07:52,244 --> 00:08:00,331
So he said to this teacher, if this termite hill has six holes and you want to get the snake out, how would you do it?

65
00:08:00,632 --> 00:08:03,995
So he said, well, you block up five holes and the snake comes out.

66
00:08:04,456 --> 00:08:06,577
And he said, that's what you must do in your meditation.

67
00:08:06,958 --> 00:08:10,401
Block out the five senses and just observe the heart-mind.

68
00:08:10,882 --> 00:08:15,487
And of course, in no length of time, the teacher became fully liberated.

69
00:08:15,547 --> 00:08:22,132
So that's the bit of a teaching here about these seven types.

70
00:08:24,627 --> 00:08:36,986
And in fact, you know, in my Zen practice, I remember them always saying if there's a hair's breadth of difference between, you know, sitting and your daily life, your daily life activity, you've lost the way.

71
00:08:37,648 --> 00:08:45,541
So our effort is always to make what we're doing something upon which we are placing our attention.

72
00:08:45,942 --> 00:08:46,623
It's wholesome.

73
00:08:46,923 --> 00:08:49,587
We're putting our attention there and that's enough.

74
00:08:53,365 --> 00:09:01,312
So then we have a very important statement when I finally get this thing going.

75
00:09:01,432 --> 00:09:01,873
Just a minute.

76
00:09:05,376 --> 00:09:15,125
Now, it's funny that this comes after these categories.

77
00:09:16,648 --> 00:09:20,812
I do not say that awakening is achieved right away.

78
00:09:21,251 --> 00:09:21,852
Rather,

79
00:09:22,423 --> 00:09:28,873
Awakening is achieved by gradual training, gradual progress and gradual practice.

80
00:09:30,895 --> 00:09:33,458
So that's important to understand is gradual.

81
00:09:33,519 --> 00:09:38,346
Now, often when we come into the practice, it's very new to us.

82
00:09:39,528 --> 00:09:46,778
And we practice what you might say with an open mind, an open heart, what Zen calls beginner's mind.

83
00:09:47,787 --> 00:09:58,604
And usually we have, you know, insights and a lifting, and it really can have an immediate effect on our lives.

84
00:09:59,846 --> 00:10:02,390
And then after a while, we keep practicing, practicing.

85
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:03,451
Nothing much happens.

86
00:10:03,893 --> 00:10:06,417
You know, we think, well, you know, where's the progress?

87
00:10:06,517 --> 00:10:07,818
Looking for progress.

88
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:12,005
Lots of meditators are seeking progress.

89
00:10:12,592 --> 00:10:17,941
And it's good to remind ourselves that, you know, this is a very gradual path.

90
00:10:17,961 --> 00:10:20,183
The Buddha says gradual, but I say very gradual.

91
00:10:21,426 --> 00:10:31,039
And if you liken it to climbing a hill or climbing a mountain, remember you start off with all that energy and that, you know, you want to get to the top.

92
00:10:31,059 --> 00:10:37,690
And then, you know, after, you know, a few minutes, even so, you can feel the heaviness in your legs.

93
00:10:38,107 --> 00:11:06,293
and you begin to think well i need a rest and you sit down and when you sit down of course you get a bit of a view and that inspires you think oh well when i get to the top there'll be this fantastic view so you keep going and then you hit this plateau and the plateau keeps going on and nothing nothing happens but you can see that in the distance there's another rise and so the spiritual life goes up like that right up plateau up plateau

94
00:11:06,863 --> 00:11:19,217
So even when you feel there's no progress, just by putting in the practice, by constantly bringing mindfulness to bear, we're moving very slowly, very gently.

95
00:11:19,498 --> 00:11:23,081
We're on the path and it will take us there.

96
00:11:23,101 --> 00:11:24,083
So that's good to remember.

97
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:30,331
Now, actually, he then says, how is this training achieved?

98
00:11:31,893 --> 00:11:35,216
When someone in whom faith has arisen approaches a teacher,

99
00:11:35,585 --> 00:11:42,975
They pay homage, lend an ear, hear the teachings, remember the teachings, reflect on their meaning and accept them after consideration.

100
00:11:44,035 --> 00:11:45,638
Their enthusiasm springs up.

101
00:11:45,658 --> 00:11:47,921
They make an effort, weigh up and persevere.

102
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:53,368
Persevering, they directly realize the ultimate truth and see it with penetrating wisdom.

103
00:11:54,769 --> 00:11:58,514
Now he turns upon these two naughty monks.

104
00:11:58,995 --> 00:12:02,200
There has not been that faith, that approaching, that paying homage.

105
00:12:02,533 --> 00:12:14,330
that listening, that hearing of teaching, that remembering of the teaching, that reflecting on their meaning, their acceptance after consideration, that enthusiasm, that making an effort, that weighing up and that striving.

106
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:18,716
You've lost the way because you're practicing in the wrong way.

107
00:12:19,277 --> 00:12:24,302
Just how far have these foolish people strayed from this teaching and training?

108
00:12:24,624 --> 00:12:30,412
So he's giving them a real beating now.

109
00:12:30,432 --> 00:12:32,254
And then he says,

110
00:12:34,866 --> 00:12:46,437
And then he points out now, look, even if a teacher who values material things is an heir to material things, who lives caught up in material things, you wouldn't get into such haggling, right?

111
00:12:46,658 --> 00:12:54,725
So even if a teacher's not very good at spiritual life or anywhere, really, you don't say, if we get this, we'll do that.

112
00:12:55,265 --> 00:12:57,668
If we don't get this, we don't do that.

113
00:12:57,688 --> 00:13:04,434
So remember, these monks were rebelling against the new rules about not eating in the evening,

114
00:13:04,650 --> 00:13:05,652
etc.

115
00:13:07,094 --> 00:13:14,524
So then he says, for a faithful disciple who is practicing to fathom the teacher's instruction, this is in line with the teaching.

116
00:13:15,164 --> 00:13:18,288
The Buddha is my teacher, I am his disciple.

117
00:13:18,389 --> 00:13:20,270
The Buddha knows, I do not know.

118
00:13:21,111 --> 00:13:28,802
For a faithful disciple who is practicing to fathom the teacher's instructions, the teacher's instructions are nourishing and nutritious.

119
00:13:29,423 --> 00:13:35,772
But a faithful disciple who is practicing to fathom the teacher's instruction, this is in line with the teaching.

120
00:13:36,253 --> 00:13:37,033
And I'll listen to this.

121
00:13:37,695 --> 00:13:43,022
Gladly let only skin, sinews and bones remain.

122
00:13:43,722 --> 00:13:46,927
Let the flesh and blood waste away in my body.

123
00:13:47,708 --> 00:13:55,919
I will not relax my energy until I have achieved what is possible by courageous strength, energy and vigour.

124
00:13:56,440 --> 00:14:03,769
A faithful disciple who is practicing to fathom the teacher's instructions can expect one of two results.

125
00:14:04,691 --> 00:14:12,783
Full liberation in this present life, or if there's something left, a non-returner, somebody who doesn't come back to be reborn here.

126
00:14:13,464 --> 00:14:14,225
So there we are.

127
00:14:14,684 --> 00:14:17,089
That's the instruction the Buddha is giving us, you see.

128
00:14:17,990 --> 00:14:22,296
Let flesh and blood waste away in my body.

129
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:31,168
I will not relax my energy until I have achieved what is possible by courageous strength, energy, and vigor.

130
00:14:32,870 --> 00:14:38,657
This is what the Buddha said, satisfied the bhikkhus were happy with what the Buddha had spoken.

131
00:14:39,097 --> 00:14:40,600
So there's the challenge, you see.

132
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:42,621
There's the challenge.

133
00:14:42,721 --> 00:14:44,303
Obviously, we want to make it easy.

134
00:14:44,323 --> 00:14:48,368
We don't want to go to the extent of losing muscle.

135
00:14:49,495 --> 00:14:58,634
So it's good to keep in mind that this practice has to be, you know, a real giving of self, a real devotion to it.

136
00:14:59,115 --> 00:15:10,136
Now, of course, the Buddha here is giving us extreme examples, but I remember when Saibhupandita invited me to come with him to Burma.

137
00:15:10,386 --> 00:15:13,791
Now, I had been to Burma before and had terrible time.

138
00:15:14,211 --> 00:15:19,999
I got amoebic dysentery and then amoebic hepatitis, like, you know, it was bad news.

139
00:15:20,659 --> 00:15:24,445
And I mentioned this to him that I was a little bit afraid of this, you see.

140
00:15:24,745 --> 00:15:29,770
And the message he sent back was, you won't get anywhere unless you're prepared to die.

141
00:15:30,312 --> 00:15:34,216
So this is the instruction by the Buddha.

142
00:15:34,417 --> 00:15:52,965
we have to give everything in order to gain everything and with that in mind let us commit ourselves to our practice and be liberated from all this terrible suffering sooner rather than later so we can do a little practice

